From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ask2(T-M6-2 B2): wire cc_pack_key_l2() into the CC install dispatch

Depends on 0204+0205 (adds src_mac/FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_MAC_SRC and
cc_pack_key_l2() this wires in).

B2 (plans/ASK2-BRIDGE-OFFLOAD-PLAN.md) is the decisive silicon de-risk
proof: hand-arm a CC leaf matching a fixed destination MAC, enqueue to
another port's TX FQ, with the miss row = FE_ENTER, and confirm on
silicon that (a) an L2 frame to that DA forwards with the CPU bypassed
and (b) an untagged routed flow on the same port still hits the ehash
path via CC-miss. Doing that needs a way to actually INSTALL such a
tree -- this patch is that plumbing, still entirely debugfs-gated and
off any live traffic path:

1. struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec gains a `bridge_l2` bool (mirrors the
   existing `dual_lane`/`dual_lane_pid` pattern exactly): when set,
   fman_pcd_cc_static_install() sizes the tree's match rows as
   CC_KEY_SIZE_L2 (15 bytes) and packs every key via cc_pack_key_l2()
   instead of the IP-oriented packers. False for every existing caller,
   so every existing CC tree (routed, VLAN single/dual-lane) stays
   byte-identical -- purely additive dispatch, no existing branch
   touched.

2. cc_pack_key_l2() itself drops __maybe_unused now that it has a real
   caller (fman_pcd_cc_static_install(), reached only when bridge_l2 is
   set -- still unreachable from any live path since nothing sets that
   flag outside the cc_test debugfs harness and its own KUnit tests).

3. fman_pcd_cc_test.c (plain-tracked, edited directly) gains a new
   `install_l2 <port> <dst_mac> <target_fqid>` debugfs command
   alongside the existing IP-oriented `install`. Auto-fills
   miss_fe_off from fman_pcd_fe_root_get_offset() -- 0 if FE_ENTER
   isn't engaged yet (a valid pure-L2-leaf state), non-zero if it is
   (the actual B2 coexistence-proof precondition: engage ASK ehash
   routing on the port first, then install_l2).

Still fully dormant: no KeyGen scheme-attach happens anywhere in this
patch, so nothing reaches an L2 leaf on any live port until the
operator both engages the port's KG scheme for L2 extraction AND
issues an explicit debugfs write -- the live-arming step itself (which
port, what scheme, what to observe) is B2's actual experiment, done by
hand on a sacrificial port, not something this patch performs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
index ccf9ea6..d02a2c2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd_cc.c
@@ -599,11 +599,14 @@ static void __maybe_unused cc_pack_key_3tuple(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
  * bytes zero (wildcard), per B1's stated gate: "KUnit vectors for
  * DA-only and PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE keys."
  *
- * __maybe_unused: not yet wired into fman_pcd_cc_bridge_key_add/remove()
- * (below) or any live install path. Pinned by
- * tests/fman_pcd_cc_l2_key_test.c.
+ * T-M6-2 B2: reachable from fman_pcd_cc_static_install() when the caller
+ * sets struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec.bridge_l2 -- but nothing in-tree does
+ * that yet outside the cc_test debugfs harness (fman_pcd_cc_test.c's
+ * install_l2 command) and the KUnit tests below, so this is still not on
+ * any live traffic path (no KeyGen scheme-attach caller exists). Pinned
+ * by tests/fman_pcd_cc_l2_key_test.c.
  */
-static void __maybe_unused cc_pack_key_l2(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
+static void cc_pack_key_l2(void __iomem *match, u16 idx,
 					  const struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_key *k)
 {
 	u8 key[CC_KEY_SIZE_L2];
@@ -902,7 +905,8 @@ int fman_pcd_cc_static_install(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
 		for (i = 0; i < hw->num_keys; i++)
 			if (hw->keys[i].present & FMAN_PCD_CC_HW_F_IPV6)
 				v6 = true;
-		t->key_size = hw->dual_lane ?
+		t->key_size = hw->bridge_l2 ? CC_KEY_SIZE_L2 :
+			hw->dual_lane ?
 			(hw->dual_lane_pid ? CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL_PID : CC_KEY_SIZE_DUAL) :
 			(v6 ? CC_KEY_SIZE_V6 : CC_KEY_SIZE);
 	}
@@ -946,7 +950,9 @@ int fman_pcd_cc_static_install(struct fman_pcd *pcd, u8 port_id,
 
 	/* Encode each key's match record + leaf result AD. */
 	for (i = 0; i < hw->num_keys; i++) {
-		if (hw->dual_lane && hw->dual_lane_pid)
+		if (hw->bridge_l2)
+			cc_pack_key_l2(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
+		else if (hw->dual_lane && hw->dual_lane_pid)
 			cc_pack_key_dual_pid(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
 		else if (hw->dual_lane)
 			cc_pack_key_dual(t->match, i, &hw->keys[i]);
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index db279b2..dd4dec7 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -631,6 +631,20 @@ struct fman_pcd_cc_hw_spec {
 				 * (this false) keeps the plain 46-byte
 				 * cc_pack_key_dual() path byte-identical.
 				 */
+	bool bridge_l2;	/* T-M6-2 B2: use the 15-byte PORT_ID|DA|SA|ETYPE
+			 * bridge FDB key (cc_pack_key_l2(), CC_KEY_SIZE_L2)
+			 * for every key in this tree, instead of the plain
+			 * IP-oriented packers. Mutually exclusive with
+			 * @dual_lane in practice (a tree is either all-IP or
+			 * all-L2, mirroring how @dual_lane itself works) --
+			 * not enforced here, caller's responsibility, same as
+			 * every other @*_lane combination. False for every
+			 * existing caller, so every existing CC tree stays
+			 * byte-identical. The port's KeyGen scheme must
+			 * separately be armed for the L2 extraction (B2/B3),
+			 * or the extracted key width/content won't match what
+			 * this tree compares.
+			 */
 };
 
 /**
